{"format":1,"seq":114,"writes":[{"type":"entry","value":{"model":[{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm spotting several recurring error patterns: gh.api throwing \"unexpected token\" errors likely from JSON parsing non-JSON output, a requirement that gh.api arguments be passed as an array, and models hallucinating a nonexistent `gh.pr` command.\n\nI also see repeated failures from missing node_modules when running tests fresh (no bootstrap step before vitest), delivery.validate hitting the same dependency mismatch, and delivery.commit allowing pushes straight to a protected main branch without guardrails. There's also pr.waitForChecks hitting its timeout ceiling without settling, and ci.waitForCommit's return type causing type errors when accessing `.conclusion`.\n\nBeyond that, workspace.edit's typed tuple and template-literal types cause friction, search result shapes are inconsistent (`.results` vs `matches`), atob isn't available for base64 decoding so file reads need another path through gh.api, shell.exec has its own default timeout, npm.run's argument signature trips things up, and tests.runTargeted needs a file path rather than a directory. I also want to check successful calls that got truncated or required repeat invocations, and look back at the earlier bash-based threads (353–363) to see if pit was even loaded then.\n\n","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_bdrk_012UWrBteM9WxezhstA2e4bk","name":"typescript","arguments":{"code":"// @pit: {\"label\": \"Show code and follow-ups for gh.api, gh.pr, push, and wait failures\"}\nasync ({ shell: { exec } }, p: { js: string }) => {\n  const s = await exec(`cat > /tmp/detail.mjs <<'EOF'\\n${p.js}\\nEOF\\nnode /tmp/detail.mjs`, { timeoutMs: 28000 });\n  return s.stdout.slice(0, 48000) + s.stderr.slice(0, 3000);\n}","params":{"js":"import fs from 'fs';\nconst calls=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('/tmp/calls.json','utf8'));\nconst want=['372#6','372#7','375#5','376#2','376#3'